# Shell scripts must stay LF — CRLF breaks Git Bash's shebang parsing and
# broke the AI-log pre-push hook on Windows checkouts (core.autocrlf=true).
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same rule, extended to everything a Linux host parses rather than a human reads. These are
# authored on Windows with core.autocrlf=true and consumed on an ARM Ubuntu VM, and CRLF has
# already cost this repo two hook bugs and a stray `.gitkeep\r`. Each of these fails in a way that
# is hard to read: Docker treats a trailing \r as part of the command, systemd rejects the unit
# with a parse error, and Caddy's directive parser breaks on the line ending.
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
Caddyfile       text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
Makefile        text eol=lf

# Committed artifacts are binary and must never be line-ending converted — a single "fixed" byte
# would silently corrupt an embedding matrix or a thumbnail.
*.npy           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.pptx          binary
*.pdf           binary

* text=auto
